  "body": "The [Adoption Agency Algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#adoption-agency-algorithm) reparents already-inserted subtrees via [append](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-append), [remove](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-remove), and [insert](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-insert), building clones detached before re-attaching them. This disconnects and reconnects live subtrees **twice**:\n- `<iframe>` descendants are destroyed and reloaded *twice*\n- Focus, open popovers, modal `<dialog>`s, CSS animations, `speculationrules`, `<img>` auto-sizes, and table-fostered `<form>` owners are reset.\n- Custom elements with `connectedMoveCallback` get two `disconnectedCallback`/`connectedCallback` pairs instead.\n\n### Proposal\n\nUse DOM's state-preserving [move](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#move) (exporting raw `move` / `ensure pre-move validity` in `whatwg/dom`) and assemble AAA clones **top-down**:\n\n1. **Move-or-reparent helper** (*node*, *parent*, *child*): bail on invalid/cyclic targets; adjust *child* if *child* is *node*; `move` if *node* has a parent and shares a [shadow-including root](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-including-root) with *parent*; otherwise `remove` (if parented) + `insert` (preserving detached/cross-document cases in [adoption-agency-reparenting.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/syntax/parsing/adoption-agency-reparenting.html)).\n2. **Inner loop + outer placement**: build the empty clone spine (*outermostClone* .. *innermostClone*) without detaching *furthestBlock*. If (*target*, *refNode*) is valid for *furthestBlock* (and *outermostClone*), move-or-reparent *outermostClone* into (*target*, *refNode*) first and then move-or-reparent *furthestBlock* into *innermostClone* (or directly into (*target*, *refNode*) if no clones); otherwise `remove` *furthestBlock* if parented.\n3. **Wrap *furthestBlock*'s children**: move-or-reparent the new *formattingElement* clone into *furthestBlock* **first**, then move-or-reparent *furthestBlock*'s preceding children into it (also fixing #12828).\n\nCustom elements without `connectedMoveCallback` still get `disconnectedCallback` + `connectedCallback` via [enqueue a custom element callback reaction](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#enqueue-a-custom-element-callback-reaction) (orthogonal to #13072).\n",
